{{- define "wake_initial_planning" -}}
This is initial planning. Read the goal spec, assess complexity, and create exactly one planning task.

AUTONOMY NOTICE:
You have FULL autonomy to run CLI commands immediately.
Do NOT wait for permission.

--- PLANNING PHASE COMPLETE. NOW EXECUTE. ---

1. Read the goal spec ({{.GoalSpecRef}}) thoroughly.
2. Assess whether the goal is simple or fan-out.
3. Create exactly one planning task.

SIMPLE GOAL:
Use the specialized planning target when the goal has one coherent planning scope: one functional area, no shared file/schema/interface ownership question, no migration or cross-cutting contract needing explicit ownership, and no expected downstream split into independent specialized scopes.

FAN-OUT OR UNCERTAIN GOAL:
Use the mapped master planning target when available if multiple functional areas need separate ownership, shared files or interfaces require explicit boundary assignment, independent downstream workstreams could run in parallel after planning, the goal would likely produce more than 8 downstream output entries, or boundary placement is uncertain.

--- EXECUTION PHASE (MANDATORY - DO NOT SKIP) ---
{{- if .GoalEntryPoint }}

Entry-point "{{.GoalEntryPoint}}" was specified. Dispatch simple goals to {{.ResolvedDisplayName}}.

Run {{binaryName}} add-tasks once with exactly one task in a JSON file.
The file must contain a bare JSON array -- NOT a wrapper object.

SIMPLE GOAL TASK EXAMPLE:
[
  {
    "id": "{{.ResolvedTaskIDPrefix}}-1",
    "desc": "<single planning scope>: <boundary description>",
    "spec": "{{.GoalSpecRef}}",
    "done": "Implementation plan for <single planning scope> is complete, reviewable, and submitted for review",
    "scope": "Planning only: <single planning scope>. No implementation.",
    "priority": 1,
    "depends": [],
    "type": "{{.ResolvedTaskType}}",
    "role_pair": "{{.ResolvedRolePair}}"
  }
]
{{- if .ResolvedHasFanOutTarget }}

Fan-out goals dispatch to {{.ResolvedFanOutDisplayName}} through the mapped master target.

FAN-OUT GOAL TASK EXAMPLE:
[
  {
    "id": "{{.ResolvedFanOutTaskIDPrefix}}-1",
    "desc": "Master planning: define the shared approach and decomposition boundaries for {{.GoalEntryPoint}}",
    "spec": "{{.GoalSpecRef}}",
    "done": "Master planning decomposition is complete, reviewable, and submitted for review",
    "scope": "Planning only: define boundaries, interface contracts, ownership, and specialized follow-up scopes. No implementation.",
    "priority": 1,
    "depends": [],
    "type": "{{.ResolvedFanOutTaskType}}",
    "role_pair": "{{.ResolvedFanOutRolePair}}"
  }
]
{{- else }}

No mapped master planning role-pair is configured for this entry-point.
Specialized fallback remains claimable by {{.ResolvedDisplayName}}.
For fan-out or uncertain goals, still create exactly one specialized planning task using the simple goal example above. Do not invent a master role-pair.
{{- end }}

Then run: {{binaryName}} add-tasks --tasks-file <path.json> --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json

SUCCESS CRITERIA:
- Exactly one task is created.
- Simple goals use role_pair {{.ResolvedRolePair}}.
{{- if .ResolvedHasFanOutTarget }}
- Fan-out or uncertain goals use role_pair {{.ResolvedFanOutRolePair}}.
{{- else }}
- Missing master mapping falls back to one task in role_pair {{.ResolvedRolePair}}.
{{- end }}
- The task is claimable by the target planning role.
{{- else if .EntryPoints }}

No entry-point was specified. Classify the input document and choose the appropriate entry-point.

AVAILABLE ENTRY-POINTS:
{{- range .EntryPoints }}
{{- if .HasFanOutTarget }}
- "{{.Name}}": simple role_pair "{{.SimpleRolePair}}", type "{{.SimpleTaskType}}", display "{{.SimpleDisplayName}}", id prefix "{{.SimpleTaskIDPrefix}}"; fan-out role_pair "{{.FanOutRolePair}}", type "{{.FanOutTaskType}}", display "{{.FanOutDisplayName}}", id prefix "{{.FanOutTaskIDPrefix}}"
{{- else }}
- "{{.Name}}": simple role_pair "{{.SimpleRolePair}}", type "{{.SimpleTaskType}}", display "{{.SimpleDisplayName}}", id prefix "{{.SimpleTaskIDPrefix}}"; fan-out unavailable, use the simple target as fallback
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

CLASSIFICATION GUIDANCE:
- Choose "functional-spec" if the document already defines product/functional requirements,
  user stories, or acceptance criteria, but still needs architecture consolidation before code planning.
- Choose "technical-spec" if the document already contains an implementation-ready technical plan
  with architecture, boundaries, and interfaces settled enough to start code planning directly.
- "detailed-spec" is a legacy alias for "functional-spec"; prefer "functional-spec" for new work.
- Choose "general-objective" for vision documents, broad objectives, or when uncertain.
  Default to "general-objective" -- skipping the spec phase is riskier than redundant refinement.

Choose the chosen entry-point's simple target for a simple goal.
Choose the chosen entry-point's fan-out target for a fan-out or uncertain goal when it is listed.
If no fan-out target is listed for the chosen entry-point, create exactly one task using its simple target.

SIMPLE GOAL TASK EXAMPLE:
[
  {
    "id": "<chosen-simple-prefix>-1",
    "desc": "<single planning scope>: <boundary description>",
    "spec": "{{.GoalSpecRef}}",
    "done": "Implementation plan for <single planning scope> is complete, reviewable, and submitted for review",
    "scope": "Planning only: <single planning scope>. No implementation.",
    "priority": 1,
    "depends": [],
    "type": "<chosen-simple-type>",
    "role_pair": "<chosen-simple-role-pair>"
  }
]

FAN-OUT GOAL TASK EXAMPLE:
[
  {
    "id": "<chosen-fan-out-prefix>-1",
    "desc": "Master planning: define the shared approach and decomposition boundaries for <chosen-entry-point>",
    "spec": "{{.GoalSpecRef}}",
    "done": "Master planning decomposition is complete, reviewable, and submitted for review",
    "scope": "Planning only: define boundaries, interface contracts, ownership, and specialized follow-up scopes. No implementation.",
    "priority": 1,
    "depends": [],
    "type": "<chosen-fan-out-type>",
    "role_pair": "<chosen-fan-out-role-pair>"
  }
]

Then run: {{binaryName}} add-tasks --tasks-file <path.json> --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json

SUCCESS CRITERIA:
- Exactly one task is created.
- Classification reasoning is stated before creating the task.
- Simple goals use the chosen simple role_pair.
- Fan-out or uncertain goals use the chosen fan-out role_pair when available.
- Missing master mappings fall back to one task in the chosen simple role_pair.
{{- else }}

Write a JSON file with exactly one planning task and run {{binaryName}} add-tasks.
The file must contain a bare JSON array -- NOT a wrapper object.
[
  {
    "id": "code-planning-1",
    "desc": "<single planning scope>: <boundary description>",
    "spec": "{{.GoalSpecRef}}",
    "done": "Implementation plan for <single planning scope> is complete, reviewable, and submitted for code-plan-review",
    "scope": "Planning only: <single planning scope>. No implementation.",
    "priority": 1,
    "depends": [],
    "type": "planning",
    "role_pair": "code-planning-pair"
  }
]
Then run: {{binaryName}} add-tasks --tasks-file <path.json> --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json

SUCCESS CRITERIA:
- Exactly one task is created.
- The task uses role_pair code-planning-pair.
- The task enters DRAFT_CODING_PLAN and is claimable by code-planner.
{{- end }}

EXPECTED BEHAVIOR EXAMPLES:
- Simple goal: one specialized planning task, no depends_on, confirm success, exit.
- Fan-out goal with a mapped master target: one master planning task, no specialized fan-out here, confirm success, exit.
- Fan-out goal without a mapped master target: one specialized planning task, no invented master role-pair, confirm success, exit.

INCORRECT:
1. Plan but do not execute {{binaryName}} add-tasks
2. Exit without creating the task
3. Add a second INITIAL_PLANNING task
4. Create downstream implementation tasks -- only planning tasks belong here
{{- end -}}
